  <running_head>Castigatio Paral.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">clesiæ, Episcopo &amp; proximo. De hac</l>
    <l n="2">disputabimus prolixius ad controver-</l>
    <l n="3">siam primam seculi VI. quando Har-</l>
    <l n="4">scherus in Hæresi Jacobinorum quæsrit;</l>
    <l n="5">An sacerdoti omnia peccata mor-</l>
    <l n="6">talia sint confessione exponenda?</l>
    <l n="7" type="heading" level="2" para="true">2. Satisfactionem, quâ pœna temporaria</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="2">mitigetur, suscipere esse impietatem.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Non est quæstio de politica satisfa-</l>
    <l n="10">ctione, quâ quis propter damnum &amp;</l>
    <l n="11">iniurias Magistratui vel proximo illatas</l>
    <l n="12">secundùm leges punitur, &amp; sic le-</l>
    <l n="13">gibus, proximoquè satisfacit. Quomodo</l>
    <l n="14">in V. T. fur, qui furatus est bovem</l>
    <l n="15">rependere debebat quinquè boves, &amp;</l>
    <l n="16">pro una pecude quatuor pecudes, quò</l>
    <l n="17">pertinent mulctæ pecuniariæ &amp; omnis</l>
    <l n="18">generis supplicia; sed de satisfactione</l>
    <l n="19">ecclesiastica &amp; canonica. Ea autem</l>
    <l n="20">est vel veteris &amp; primitivæ ecclesiæ,</l>
    <l n="21">vel novæ papisticæ.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Veteris &amp; primitivæ ecclesiæ satis-</l>
    <l n="23">factio erat, cùm illi, qui gravissimè ma-</l>
    <l n="24">gnoquè</l>
  </main_text>
